{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And Moses spoke to them</b> — this is the language of the ongoing present; the entire passage [that follows] describes the continuing practice. <b>And afterward they drew near</b> — according to Rashi's formulation (Rashi on Exodus 34:32), after he taught the elders, he would return and teach the passage or the law to Israel. But this is not so. Rather, Scripture says that when all Israel went out to meet him, they saw the rays of glory and feared to approach him, and they drew back. Perhaps they thought that the glory of HaShem was there, or angels of the Most High were with him, and they feared lest HaShem break forth against them. And Moses called to them, and Aaron and all the leaders who walked before them returned to him, and Moses spoke to them words of peace and brought them the tidings of the forgiveness of their sin and of the tablets he had brought down. And afterward all the children of Israel saw that he was speaking with the leaders, and they all drew near before him, and then he commanded them <b>all that HaShem had spoken with him on Mount Sinai</b> — and this is the second Decalogue that He gave him, and all that was said to him from the beginning: \"Observe for yourself what I command you today\" (Exodus 34:11) until the end of the passage (Exodus 34:26) — for he told them that He had commanded him to make a new covenant with them on the basis of these matters, and Scripture abbreviated this and recounted the matter in summary. And afterward it says (Exodus 34:33) that when he finished speaking with them all the aforementioned matter, he put a veil on his face — for he observed upon their retreat that the skin of his face shone, or they told him. And after he recounted the events of that day, it says <b>And when Moses came</b> (Exodus 34:34), and this is the ongoing practice, to say that he conducted himself thus with them all his days:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:54.186567634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}